<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mumtaz Mahal returns at 17 weeks 2 days. The cell-free DNA result came back low risk. She has taken ferrous sulfate every other morning for four weeks but has missed about half the doses because of nausea and constipation, and she is still tired and breathless on the stairs. She takes aspirin 81 mg at bedtime without bruising or bleeding, and folic acid. She has no headache, visual change, abdominal pain, bleeding, or urinary symptoms, and has begun to feel the baby move. She saw Dr. Montgomery-Rahimi of maternal-fetal medicine this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Screening</td><td>Cell-free DNA low risk for trisomies 21, 18, and 13</td></tr><tr><td>Iron</td><td>About half of the oral iron doses taken; nausea and constipation</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Tired; breathless on stairs; no bleeding, headache, or pain</td></tr><tr><td>Fetal movement</td><td>First movements felt</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

